{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00493",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 1.46,
      "duration_seconds": 0.86,
      "text": "Afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 3.78,
      "end_seconds": 6.83,
      "duration_seconds": 3.05,
      "text": "Right on time. Sit, please. How can I help?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 7.97,
      "end_seconds": 21.33,
      "duration_seconds": 13.36,
      "text": "So the thing is, I've got a throbbing headache on one side. I'd rather know what's going on than keep guessing. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.07,
      "end_seconds": 25.43,
      "duration_seconds": 3.36,
      "text": "Is this recent, or has it been a while?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.77,
      "end_seconds": 27.63,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "Probably about two weeks. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.96,
      "end_seconds": 36.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.78,
      "end_seconds": 44.74,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "It comes and goes. Yes, loud noise and bright lights. That makes it worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 47.15,
      "end_seconds": 49.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Does it come along with anything else?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 50.79,
      "end_seconds": 56.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.91,
      "text": "Vomiting goes along with it, most of the time. The vomiting? That's been since this morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 57.6,
      "end_seconds": 60.95,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "Let me just pull up your file for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 61.71,
      "end_seconds": 62.41,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.54,
      "end_seconds": 73.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any double vision or loss of consciousness at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.67,
      "end_seconds": 78.4,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "I haven't had double vision or loss of consciousness, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.48,
      "end_seconds": 96.02,
      "duration_seconds": 16.54,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.46,
      "end_seconds": 99.51,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 100.49,
      "end_seconds": 104.25,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Alright, any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.07,
      "end_seconds": 120.17,
      "duration_seconds": 15.1,
      "text": "Escitalopram. I take it 10 milligrams, once a day. Paracetamol. I take it 500 milligrams, when needed. It's a relief to finally sit down and talk about it. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 121.57,
      "end_seconds": 124.61,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Moving on to your background, any past medical history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 125.66,
      "end_seconds": 128.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "I have anxiety, for two years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.93,
      "end_seconds": 134.91,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "What about allergies, to medicines or foods or anything else? It helps to be thorough at this stage."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 136.22,
      "end_seconds": 138.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.01,
      "text": "Not that I know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.01,
      "end_seconds": 141.94,
      "duration_seconds": 2.93,
      "text": "Is it okay if I type while we talk?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.06,
      "end_seconds": 148.11,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Yes, of course, go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.38,
      "end_seconds": 152.32,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.76,
      "end_seconds": 154.71,
      "duration_seconds": 0.95,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 155.61,
      "end_seconds": 157.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.89,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 173.77,
      "end_seconds": 176.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.64,
      "text": "Neck is supple, no stiffness at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 180.85,
      "end_seconds": 199.93,
      "duration_seconds": 19.08,
      "text": "All done, thank you, please sit down. Good, that's all I need to examine. Let me gather my thoughts and then we'll talk it through together. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with migraine with aura. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 201.36,
      "end_seconds": 203.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.36,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 205.25,
      "end_seconds": 222.88,
      "duration_seconds": 17.63,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like migraine with aura, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a throbbing headache on one side for about two weeks, and no loss of consciousness or double vision."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 223.36,
      "end_seconds": 224.56,
      "duration_seconds": 1.2,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 225.26,
      "end_seconds": 241.37,
      "duration_seconds": 16.11,
      "text": "What I'm doing here is putting together three things: what you tell me, what I find when I examine you, and what the tests show. None of those alone is enough, which is why we sometimes need to wait for results before being certain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.72,
      "end_seconds": 243.71,
      "duration_seconds": 1.99,
      "text": "I appreciate you explaining that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 244.59,
      "end_seconds": 253.64,
      "duration_seconds": 9.05,
      "text": "Let's get an MRI of the brain, for recurrent headaches. I'd rather check than guess, and this is the quickest way to know more."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 254.26,
      "end_seconds": 256.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "Sure, where do I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.07,
      "end_seconds": 282.34,
      "duration_seconds": 24.27,
      "text": "Let's use sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, at the start of an attack, as needed. You take it by mouth. It's for migraine. Try not to skip meals and keep your sleep regular. Keep a headache diary, things like skipped meals, poor sleep, certain foods and the weather. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 283.18,
      "end_seconds": 292.6,
      "duration_seconds": 9.42,
      "text": "If you have the worst headache of your life or any weakness, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 295.07,
      "end_seconds": 295.77,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Understood."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 297.17,
      "end_seconds": 304.82,
      "duration_seconds": 7.65,
      "text": "Let's review you in a month. I want to be sure we're on the same page. How would you describe the plan?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 305.95,
      "end_seconds": 314.23,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "So, I take the sumatriptan, 50 milligrams, at the start of an attack and come back in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 314.95,
      "end_seconds": 319.42,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Take care, and don't hesitate to call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.21,
      "end_seconds": 322.84,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Nothing more from me, doctor, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 325.38,
      "end_seconds": 327.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.17,
      "text": "Bye for now, look after yourself."
    }
  ]
}